{
    "map": {
        "description": "Analyzes obstacle data and obstruction identification surfaces (OIS) to determine if obstacles are penetrating.",
        "elevation_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>The field containing base elevation heights of the obstacle features.</p><p>This parameter is active if the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Obstacle Features</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Relative height</span> and the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Elevations</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Elevation field</span>. The default is the first numeric field in the obstacle feature class.</p></xdoc>",
        "elevation_field.title": "Elevation Field",
        "elevation_field_unit.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the linear unit that will be used for the base elevation values. This parameter is active if the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Obstacle Features</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Relative height</span> and the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Elevations</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Elevation field</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.CENTIMETERS": "Centimeters",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.DECIMAL_DEGREES": "Decimal degrees",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.DECIMETERS": "Decimeters",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.FEET": "Feet",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.INCHES": "Inches",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.KILOMETERS": "Kilometers",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.METERS": "Meters",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.MILES": "Miles",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.MILLIMETERS": "Millimeters",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.NAUTICAL_MILES": "Nautical miles",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.POINTS": "Points",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.UNKNOWN": "Unknown",
        "elevation_field_unit.domain.YARDS": "Yards",
        "elevation_field_unit.title": "Elevation Field Units",
        "elevation_option.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies how obstacle base elevation heights will be identified. This parameter is active if the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Obstacle Features</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Relative height</span>.</p><ul><li><span title=\"ELEVATION_FIELD\">Elevation field</span>— Base elevation heights will be derived from a numeric field of the obstacle feature class. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"ELEVATION_DEM\">Elevation DEM</span>— Base elevation heights will be derived from one or more digital elevation models (DEMs).</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "elevation_option.domain.ELEVATION_DEM": "Elevation DEM",
        "elevation_option.domain.ELEVATION_FIELD": "Elevation field",
        "elevation_option.title": "Elevations",
        "height_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>The field containing the height of the obstacle features. The default value is <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Feature Geometry</span>.</p><ul><li><span title=\"FEATURE_GEOMETRY\">Feature Geometry</span>—The field containing the height of the obstacle features.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "height_field.domain.FEATURE_GEOMETRY": "Feature Geometry",
        "height_field.title": "Obstacle Height",
        "height_option.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies how obstacle height values will be interpreted.</p><ul><li><span title=\"ABSOLUTE_HEIGHT\">Absolute height</span>— Obstacle heights will be measured from sea level. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"RELATIVE_HEIGHT\">Relative height</span>— Obstacle heights will be measured from ground level.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "height_option.domain.ABSOLUTE_HEIGHT": "Absolute height",
        "height_option.domain.RELATIVE_HEIGHT": "Relative height",
        "height_option.title": "Obstacle Features",
        "in_dems.descr": "<xdoc><p>The DEMs covering the obstacles that will be used to derive base elevation values. This parameter is active if the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Obstacle Features</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Relative height</span> and the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Elevations</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Elevation DEM</span>.</p></xdoc>",
        "in_dems.title": "Input Elevation Model",
        "input_obstacle_features.descr": "The input obstacle features that will be analyzed. The feature class must be z-enabled.",
        "input_obstacle_features.title": "Input Obstacle Features",
        "input_ois_features.descr": "The multipatch features with defined Airport schema. The feature class must be z-enabled.",
        "input_ois_features.title": "Input OIS Features",
        "out_feature_class.descr": "A feature class containing one point for each obstacle feature that is within the area covered by the input OIS. If the geometry type of the input obstacle feature is a polyline or polygon, a multipoint feature class will be created.",
        "out_feature_class.title": "Output Obstacle Feature Class",
        "summary": "<xdoc><p>Analyzes obstacle data and obstruction identification surfaces (OIS) to determine if obstacles are penetrating.</p><p>To learn more about the tool, refer to the ArcGIS Pro Shorts video, Analyze Runway Obstacles in ArcGIS.</p></xdoc>",
        "title": "Analyze Runway Obstacles",
        "unit_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies the linear unit that will be used for the obstacle height. This parameter is active if the <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Obstacle Features</span> parameter is set to <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Relative height</span>.</p><ul><li><span title=\"KILOMETERS\">Kilometers</span>—The linear unit will be kilometers.</li><li><span title=\"METERS\">Meters</span>—The linear unit will be meters.</li><li><span title=\"DECIMETERS\">Decimeters</span>—The linear unit will be decimeters.</li><li><span title=\"CENTIMETERS\">Centimeters</span>—The linear unit will be centimeters.</li><li><span title=\"MILLIMETERS\">Millimeters</span>—The linear unit will be millimeters.</li><li><span title=\"NAUTICAL_MILES\">Nautical miles</span>—The linear unit will be nautical miles.</li><li><span title=\"MILES\">Miles</span>—The linear unit will be miles.</li><li><span title=\"YARDS\">Yards</span>—The linear unit will be yards.</li><li><span title=\"FEET\">Feet</span>—The linear unit will be feet.</li><li><span title=\"INCHES\">Inches</span>—The linear unit will be inches.</li><li><span title=\"DECIMAL_DEGREES\">Decimal degrees</span>—The linear unit will be decimal degrees.</li><li><span title=\"POINTS\">Points</span>—The linear unit will be points.</li><li><span title=\"UNKNOWN\">Unknown</span>—The linear unit will be unknown.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "unit_field.domain.CENTIMETERS": "Centimeters",
        "unit_field.domain.DECIMAL_DEGREES": "Decimal degrees",
        "unit_field.domain.DECIMETERS": "Decimeters",
        "unit_field.domain.FEET": "Feet",
        "unit_field.domain.INCHES": "Inches",
        "unit_field.domain.KILOMETERS": "Kilometers",
        "unit_field.domain.METERS": "Meters",
        "unit_field.domain.MILES": "Miles",
        "unit_field.domain.MILLIMETERS": "Millimeters",
        "unit_field.domain.NAUTICAL_MILES": "Nautical miles",
        "unit_field.domain.POINTS": "Points",
        "unit_field.domain.UNKNOWN": "Unknown",
        "unit_field.domain.YARDS": "Yards",
        "unit_field.title": "Unit"
    }
}
